 tu_title:'Learn Magister',tu_prev:'← Previous',tu_next:'Next →',tu_start:'Start the guided game',tu_step:'Step {0} of {1}',
 tu_s1_t:'The goal',tu_s1_x:'You lead a medieval university. You score victory points (VP) by playing Books, fulfilling Emeritus objectives, appointing a Rector and through some Cities. As soon as a player reaches 8 VP, the round is completed: most VP wins. Ties: Rector, then number of Emeritus, Professors, Students. The first player is drawn at random.',
 tu_s2_t:'Your university',tu_s2_x:'Your characters climb the ranks: Student → Professor → Emeritus, or Professor → Rector. Only Professors use their ability during Activations. Cards sit in a queue: their position (1, 2, 3…) sets part of the promotion cost, hence the value of “reorganizing”.',
 tu_s3_t:'Your turn in 3 steps',tu_s3_x:'A. Hire a Student from the row: its influence cost is shown above the card (5, 4, 3, 2, 0 and 0). You get its hiring bonus (top-left column of the card). B. Choose: Activation OR Promotion. Once you choose Promotion, you must carry it out; if no promotion is possible, the Activation happens directly. C. The row slides right and a new card arrives on the left.',
 tu_s4_t:'Activation',tu_s4_x:'Below the hiring bonus, the cap shows a type ([A] Artist, [M] Merchant, [N] Noble, [R] Religious). Activating that type first triggers your board ability, then, left to right, each Professor whose ribbons (bottom of the card) show that type.',
 tu_s5_t:'Promotion',tu_s5_x:'[stu] Student → [prof] Professor: 3 [coin] + X [infl]. [prof] Professor → [emer] Emeritus: 6 [coin] + X [infl]. [prof] Professor → [rect] Rector: 8 [infl] + X [coin] (X = position in the queue). One Rector per player and per type: it is worth 1 VP and grants a permanent power. These costs and your board\'s activation bonus are recalled below your university.',
 tu_s6_t:'Journeys',tu_s6_x:'Three journeys are drawn at random out of nine, including the Silk Road. Each movement moves one of your three [trav] Travelers one space. Reaching a City gives you its bonus. A journey is completed on space 12: the [trav] Traveler has finished its journey.',
 tu_s7_t:'Books and Letters',tu_s7_x:'Click a Book in your hand to play it (1 VP if its condition is met) or discard it for its small bonus. You may keep only 3 Books at the end of your turn: a bubble reminds you. Letters give a bonus or a Work of Art, placed on the Student hired this turn.',
 tu_s8_t:'Emeritus objectives',tu_s8_x:'Each type has its objective. As soon as you have an Emeritus of that type and meet the condition, you take the token: 3 VP for the first, 2 VP afterwards. The app claims them automatically for you.',
 tu_s9_t:'Reading the board',tu_s9_x:'Hover over a Student, a Book, a City, a Rector or an Emeritus objective to read its effect in plain words. Click an image to enlarge it (except in the row, where a click hires). The “Undo” button takes back your last decision as long as no card has been drawn, and the Log sums up everyone\'s actions.',tour_1_t:'The players',tour_1_x:'Here are the players and their victory points. As soon as a player reaches 8 VP, the round is completed.',tour_2_t:'The Rectors',tour_2_x:'One Rector tile per type. Promoting a Professor to Rector gives 1 VP and the tile\'s power. Hover over a tile to read its effect.',tour_3_t:'Emeritus objectives',tour_3_x:'One objective per type. With an Emeritus of the right type and the condition met, you gain the VP on top of the stack (3, then 2). The app awards them automatically.',tour_4_t:'The decks',tour_4_x:'The Student deck and the Book deck, with the number of cards left.',tour_5_t:'The Student row',tour_5_x:'On your turn, click a highlighted card to hire the Student. Its influence cost is in the seal above. Hover over a card to read its effects.',tour_6_t:'Journeys',tour_6_x:'Your three Travelers (horses in your color) move along these journeys. Illustrated spaces are Cities: hover over them to see their bonus. When you must move, the possible space lights up: click it.',tour_7_t:'Universities',tour_7_x:'One tab per player: click it to look at an opponent\'s university.',tour_8_t:'Your summary',tour_8_x:'Coins, influence, VP and where they come from, Traveler progress, number of characters by type and level, and works of art.',tour_9_t:'Your characters',tour_9_x:'Emeritus, Professors and Students, in queues. The number on each card is its position: it is part of the promotion cost.',tour_10_t:'Reminder',tour_10_x:'Promotion costs and your board\'s activation bonus, always in view.',tour_11_t:'Your Books',tour_11_x:'Click a Book to play it (outlined in green: condition met, +1 VP) or discard it for its bonus. Hover over it to read its condition. At most 3 Books at the end of your turn.',tour_12_t:'Letters',tour_12_x:'Some effects let you take a Letter: a resource, or a work of art placed on the Student you just hired.',tour_13_t:'The log',tour_13_x:'Everything that happened, including the AI\'s actions.',tour_14_t:'Your decisions',tour_14_x:'Choices appear here: starting pair, resources, Activation or Promotion… The “Undo” button takes back your last decision.',tour_15_t:'Home',tour_15_x:'Your game is saved: you can go back home and resume it later. Your turn now: tips will guide you during the game.',tour_btn:'Start the guided tour',tour_t:'Guided tour of the interface',tour_intro:'A real game against the AI: bubbles introduce each area of the screen, then tips guide you as you play.',tu_rules:'The rules in brief',tour_next:'Next →',tour_prev:'←',tour_skip:'Skip the tour',tour_done:'My turn!',
 tu_coach:'Tip',tip_ok:'Got it',tip_hide:'Hide tips',
 tip_pair:'To start, choose a pair of Students. You get the hiring bonuses of both cards.',
 tip_place:'One of them becomes a Professor. Pick the one whose ability (bottom of the card) you like best: it is used during Activations.',
 tip_setupBook:'Click the Book you want to discard: you gain its small bonus. Keep the one whose condition looks easiest.',
 tip_turn:'Your turn: click a highlighted Student to hire it. Its influence cost is shown above the card: the rightmost ones are free.',
 tip_choice:'Activation: your Professors of the given type produce their bonuses. Promotion: raise a character by paying its cost. Early on, activating often yields more. Careful: once you choose Promotion, you must do it.',
 tip_ci:'Pick the resource you need most: coins are mainly for promotions, influence for hiring.',
 tip_move:'Choose which Traveler moves. Aim for the Cities (illustrated spaces) whose bonus helps you.',
 tip_promo:'Choose the promotion. The cost depends on the card\'s position in its queue: position 1 is the cheapest.',
 tip_letter:'“Work of Art” Letters go on the Student you just hired and count for objectives and Books.',
 tip_reorg:'Reorganizing lets you put a card in position 1 to promote it more cheaply.',
 tip_end:'End of your turn: if a Book is outlined in green, click it to play it (1 VP)! Otherwise, end the turn.',
 tip_take:'This card lets you take one of the cheapest Students of the row for free.',
 tip_elim:'Discard another of your Students that you no longer need to get the card\'s effect.',
